course: dictionary
lesson: 1932
title: Finding meaning from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A commander is the person in charge. Words near it, such as soldiers, ship, mission or police, are the clues that show which kind of commander is meant.
explain: In «Naaman, a foreign army commander», the words army and foreign tell you he leads soldiers and comes from another country. Swap in your meaning, "a person in charge of soldiers," and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Commander can also be a title, like «Commander Smith», or a rank in some navies and in the London police. A capital letter and a name are clues that it is a title and not just a job.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Commander» means a person in charge of soldiers, a ship, an aircraft, a mission or a police operation.
fact: As a title, «Commander» is a rank in some navies and in the London police, as in «Commander Smith».
fact: Neil Armstrong was the commander of Apollo 11, the mission that first landed people on the Moon.
fact: A «hetman» was the Cossacks' chosen commander, so a hetman was the leader the Cossacks picked to lead them.
exercise: In «Naaman, a foreign army commander», what does commander mean? | A servant who cleans the tents | A visitor who likes to swim | A fast horse | *A person in charge of soldiers
exercise: Which phrase uses commander as a title, not a job? | Army commander | Ship commander | *Commander Smith | Mission commander
exercise: «A hetman was the Cossacks' chosen commander.» What does this tell you about a hetman? | A cook for the soldiers | A king's son | *A leader chosen to command the Cossacks | A ship's captain
test: In 1969, Neil Armstrong was the commander of which mission? | A school trip | *Apollo 11 | A rocket engine test | A Moon rock study
test: Which word in «Naaman, a foreign army commander» is the best clue that commander means a leader of soldiers? | foreign | a | Naaman | *army
exam: Which phrase uses commander as a title? | Hetman commander | Army commander | *Commander Smith | Mission commander
